problem:
$$
\text{(Tìm } \lim_{x \to 1} \frac{x^{n+1} - (n+1)x + n}{(x-1)^2}, n \in \mathbb{N}
$$

answer:
Đặt:
$$
\begin{cases}
S_n = \min \{x_n, y_n, z_n\} \\
f_n = \max \{x_n, y_n, z_n\}
\end{cases}
\quad (n \ge 0)
$$

Từ giả thiết, dễ thấy rằng:

$$
\begin{cases}
t_{n+1} \le t_n + \frac{1}{S_n} & (1) \\
S_{n+1} \ge S_n + \frac{1}{t_n} & (\forall n \ge 0)
\end{cases}
$$

$$
\begin{align*}
& \left\{ \begin{array}{l} S_n \ge S_o \\ \frac{t_{n+1}}{S_{n+1}} \le \frac{t_n}{S_n} \end{array} \right. \quad (\forall n \ge 0) \\
\Rightarrow & \quad \frac{t_n}{v_n} \le \frac{t_o}{v_o}, \quad \forall n \ge 0
\end{align*}
$$

Vì vậy, từ (1) và (2) suy ra:

$$
\begin{align*}
& \cdot t_n^2 \le t_{n-1}^2 + \frac{1}{S_{n-1}^2} + 2 \frac{t_{n-1}}{S_{n-1}} \\
& \le t_{n-1}^2 + \frac{1}{S_o^2} + 2 \frac{t_o}{S_o}, \quad \forall n \ge 1 \\
& \Rightarrow S_n^2 \le t_o^2 + n \left( \frac{2t_o}{S_o} + \frac{1}{S_o^2} \right), \quad \forall n \ge 1
\end{align*}
$$

$$
\begin{align*}
&\Rightarrow t_n^2 \le n \left( t_o + \frac{1}{S_o} \right)^2, \quad \forall n \ge 1 \\
&\Rightarrow t_n \le \sqrt{n} \left( t_o + \frac{1}{S_o} \right), \quad \forall n \ge 1 \tag{3}
\end{align*}
$$

$$
\begin{align*}
& \bullet S_n^2 \ge S_{n-1}^2 + 2 \frac{S_{n-1}}{S_{n-1}} + \frac{1}{t_{n-1}^2} \ge \\
& \phantom{\bullet S_n^2 \ge} > S_{n-1}^2 + 2 \frac{S_o}{t_o}, \quad \forall n \ge 1 \\
& \Rightarrow S_n^2 > S_o^2 + 2n \frac{S_o}{t_o}, \quad \forall n \ge 1 \\
& \Rightarrow S_n > \sqrt{n} \sqrt{\frac{2S_o}{t_o}} \quad (4)
\end{align*}
$$

Do: $S_n \le x_n \le t_n, \forall n \ge 1$

nên từ (3) và (4) suy ra:

$$
\sqrt{n} \sqrt{\frac{2S_o}{t_o}} \le x_n \le \sqrt{n} \left( t_o + \frac{1}{S_o} \right), \forall n \ge 1
$$

Hay $S\sqrt{n} \le x_n \le t\sqrt{n}, \forall n \ge 1$

$$
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
S = \sqrt{\frac{2S_o}{t_o}} \\
t = t_o + \frac{1}{S_o}
\end{array}
\right.
$$

